From: Maksim Sisov <msisov@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:37:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/48] Reland "extensions: Absorb the mime_types_handler
 warning into all hosts"

This is a reland of commit 704e0e99130ff84afaa01ea493a6371e5322a2d1

Original change's description:
> extensions: Absorb the mime_types_handler warning into all hosts
>
> An extension that already has host permissions for every site updates
> to a version that adds the mime_types_handler manifest key. Chrome
> disables it until the user re-approves, and the install prompt and
> chrome://management each show a separate "Read and display PDF files"
> line beside the all-sites warning. The all-hosts warning rule does not
> cover the MIME handler permission.
>
> Fix by adding the permission to that rule.
>
> Test: unit_tests --gtest_filter='PermissionMessageCombinationsUnittest.MimeTypesHandler*:PermissionsTest.IsPrivilegeIncrease:ExtensionServiceTest.MimeTypesHandler*'
> Bug: 553138801
> Change-Id: Id31070f1a762639ddae5b4bdf7f9cd38aa26f822
>
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8399134
> Reviewed-by: Devlin Cronin <rdevlin.cronin@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Maksim Sisov <msisov@igalia.com>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1712058}

